The final content_shell link fails with:

    undefined reference to
      `ui::TouchHandleDrawableAura::TouchHandleDrawableAura(aura::Window*)'
    undefined reference to `ui::TouchSelectionMenuRunner::GetInstance()'

content/browser/renderer_host/input/touch_selection_controller_client_aura.cc
is built here (it is in content/browser's unconditional source list and this
port sets use_aura = true), but the two classes it uses live behind
`if (use_aura && toolkit_views)` in ui/touch_selection, and this port sets
toolkit_views = false.

The toolkit_views half of that condition is not load-bearing for these two
files: touch_handle_drawable_aura.cc includes only aura, aura_extra, ui/base,
ui/events, ui/gfx and ui/resources, and touch_selection_menu_runner.cc
includes only its own header and base/check_op.h. Neither reaches into views,
and the deps the block adds (skia, aura, aura_extra, compositor, gfx,
resources) are all already built for this configuration.

